t`: Manages middlewares for schedule execution, including filters."},"269":{"id":"/extend/schedules-12","page_id":"/extend/schedules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/extend/schedules#schedule-system-components","content":"`ScheduleErrorHandler`: Handles middleware and schedule execution errors."},"270":{"id":"/extend/schedules-13","page_id":"/extend/schedules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/extend/schedules#registration-and-lifecycle","content":"When you add a schedule, the `ScheduleManager` stores it in the `ScheduleRepository`, asks the `ScheduleExecutionScheduler` to create a job, and then emits `ScheduleEventEnum.ScheduleAdd`. Removing a schedule follows the same coordination path in reverse and emits `ScheduleEventEnum.ScheduleRemove`."},"271":{"id":"/extend/schedules-14","page_id":"/extend/schedules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/extend/schedules#runtime-execution","content":"When the job fires, the `ScheduleJobAdapter` hands control to the `ScheduleExecutor`, which checks middlewares, executes the schedule's `tick()` method, and forwards errors to the configured `ScheduleErrorHandler`."},"272":{"id":"/extend/schedules-15","page_id":"/extend/schedules","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/extend/schedules#runtime-execution","content":"Next, see the documentation of each component, where you'll find what it does and how to replace it."},"273":{"id":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler","page_id":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler","type":"page","content":"Execution Scheduler","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Extend","Schedules"],"tags":[],"url":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler"},"274":{"id":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler-0","page_id":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler#when-to-override","content":"When to override"},"275":{"id":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-scheduler-1","page_id":"/extend/schedules/schedule-execution-