"content":"A permission filter that checks if the user has the required permissions to interact with the session."},"516":{"id":"/session","page_id":"/session","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin"],"tags":[],"url":"/session"},"517":{"id":"/session-0","page_id":"/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session#quick-example","content":"Quick example"},"518":{"id":"/session-1","page_id":"/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session#installation","content":"Installation"},"519":{"id":"/session-2","page_id":"/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session#installing","content":"Installing"},"520":{"id":"/session-3","page_id":"/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session#registering","content":"Registering"},"521":{"id":"/session-4","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"The `@nyx-discord/plugin-sessions` package is an official plugin that provides and manages user interaction sessions."},"522":{"id":"/session-5","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"These are objects that represent an open interaction \"session\" with a user. You can consider them as a more advanced, opinionated, OOP version of DJS' Interaction Collectors."},"523":{"id":"/session-6","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"They can be used as an easy way to maintain a \"conversation\" with a user, and respond to interactions that the user makes to it."},"524":{"id":"/session-7","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"Some examples of sessions are:"},"525":{"id":"/session-8","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"A paginated message that shows a user's moderations, allowing advanced options like filtering by type."},"526":{"id":"/session-9","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"An interactive message that guides a user step by step to accomplish something, like creating a ticket category."},"527":{"id":"/session-10","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"A detailed settings message that allows a user to change their server's settings with buttons, modals or select menus."},"528":{"id":"/session-11","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session","content":"In essence, any kind of situation where continuous interaction with a user is needed."},"529":{"id":"/session-12","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"This example features many components used in the same session. Some required component properties are omitted for brevity."},"530":{"id":"/session-13","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"Then somewhere in your code, like inside a command:"},"531":{"id":"/session-14","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"After filling the modal and components with values, this will look like this:"},"532":{"id":"/session-15","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"Your browser does not support the video tag."},"533":{"id":"/session-16","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"Notice how:"},"534":{"id":"/session-17","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"The plugin routes interactions belonging to the session to the appropiate handler."},"535":{"id":"/session-18","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"The session finishes automatically after the `ttl` has passed since the last interaction."},"536":{"id":"/session-19","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"The session starter is able to wait for the session to end, and then do what it needs to, like reply further."},"537":{"id":"/session-20","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#quick-example","content":"We'll dive deeper on what each of the methods do later, but this should be enough to give you an idea of how sessions work."},"538":{"id":"/session-21","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#registering","content":"Instantiate and register it to your bot's plugin manager:"},"539":{"id":"/session-22","page_id":"/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session#registering","content":"And you're done! Check the session types guides to learn how to make your own Session."},"540":{"id":"/session/limits","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"page","content":"Limits","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin","Other"],"tags":[],"url":"/session/limits"},"541":{"id":"/session/limits-0","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#registration","content":"Registration"},"542":{"id":"/session/limits-1","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#scopes","content":"Scopes"},"543":{"id":"/session/limits-2","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#user","content":"User"},"544":{"id":"/session/limits-3","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#guild","content":"Guild"},"545":{"id":"/session/limits-4","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#channel","content":"Channel"},"546":{"id":"/session/limits-5","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#composite","content":"Composite"},"547":{"id":"/session/limits-6","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#custom","content":"Custom"},"548":{"id":"/session/limits-7","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#actions","content":"Actions"},"549":{"id":"/session/limits-8","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#error","content":"Error"},"550":{"id":"/session/limits-9","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#displace","content":"Displace"},"551":{"id":"/session/limits-10","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#custom-1","content":"Custom"},"552":{"id":"/session/limits-11","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#predicates","content":"Predicates"},"553":{"id":"/session/limits-12","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#inheritance","content":"Inheritance"},"554":{"id":"/session/limits-13","page_id":"/session/limits","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/limits#multiple-rules","content":"Multiple Rules"},"555":{"id":"/session/limits-14","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits","content":"Session limits cap how many concurrent sessions a user, guild, or channel can have for a given session type.\nThey are enforced **before** a session starts, and they are registered externally via `plugin.getSessionLimits().register(...)`."},"556":{"id":"/session/limits-15","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits","content":"Limits must be registered and removed **before** starting. Calling `register()` or `remove()` after starting the bot throws an `IllegalStateError`."},"557":{"id":"/session/limits-16","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#registration","content":"Register limits through `plugin.getSessionLimits().register()` before starting the plugin. You can use either a plain object or a builder."},"558":{"id":"/session/limits-17","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#registration","content":"You can pass multiple limits to a single `register()` call and register as many limits as needed before the plugin starts."},"559":{"id":"/session/limits-18","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#scopes","content":"A scope determines which sessions count toward the limit. Each scope computes a string key from the session's starting interaction."},"560":{"id":"/session/limits-19","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#user","content":"One session per user. Multiple users can each have their own session."},"561":{"id":"/session/limits-20","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#user","content":"**Example:** An interactive `/counter` command. A user opens a session with increment/decrement buttons.\nLimit of 1 per user prevents duplicate counter sessions, and opening a second counter silently displaces the first."},"562":{"id":"/session/limits-21","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#guild","content":"One session per guild. DMs are grouped under the key `'dm'`."},"563":{"id":"/session/limits-22","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#guild","content":"**Example:** A ticket wizard. The wizard walks the user through category, priority, and description steps. Limit of 3 per guild prevents a noisy server from spawning dozens of incomplete wizards."},"564":{"id":"/session/limits-23","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#channel","content":"One session per channel. Sessions without a `channelId` get the key `'unknown'` (at the time of writing, never the case,\nbut it's still covered for future-proofing)."},"565":{"id":"/session/limits-24","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#channel","content":"**Example:** A live poll session with reaction buttons. Limit of 1 per channel ensures only one active poll runs in a channel at a time."},"566":{"id":"/session/limits-25","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#composite","content":"Combine multiple scopes. For example, one session per user per guild:"},"567":{"id":"/session/limits-26","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#composite","content":"**Example:** An embedded game like tic-tac-toe. Limit of 1 per user per guild. A user can play one game in each server they're in, but not two games in the same server."},"568":{"id":"/session/limits-27","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom","content":"Provide an arbitrary function that returns a string key:"},"569":{"id":"/session/limits-28","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom","content":"**Example:** A translation-review session. Users with the same Discord locale share one review session across the\nbot, and only one reviewer per language at a time."},"570":{"id":"/session/limits-29","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#actions","content":"An action defines what happens when the limit is exceeded."},"571":{"id":"/session/limits-30","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#error","content":"Throws `SessionLimitExceededError`, which you can catch and reply to the user:"},"572":{"id":"/session/limits-31","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#error","content":"**Example:** A profile setup wizard with max 1 per user. The second attempt throws, and the handler catches to reply with a friendly ephemeral message."},"573":{"id":"/session/limits-32","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#displace","content":"Evicts an existing session to make room. The displaced session receives `SessionEndCodes.Displaced`."},"574":{"id":"/session/limits-33","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#displace","content":"The existing session is only ended **after** the new one has started. If the new session doesn't start (its start filter\nrejects it, a middleware stops it, or its `onStart()` throws), the existing session keeps running. Only running sessions\nare displaced: if every session in the scope is still starting, the new one is rejected with `SessionLimitExceededError`."},"575":{"id":"/session/limits-34","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#displace","content":"**Example:** An interactive counter. The user runs `/counter`, and if one already exists, it's silently replaced.\nThe old session's `onEnd()` fires, its buttons are disabled, and the promise resolves with `SessionEndCodes.Displaced`."},"576":{"id":"/session/limits-35","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom-1","content":"Full control via `ExceedDecision`:"},"577":{"id":"/session/limits-36","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom-1","content":"`{ proceed: false }`: throws `SessionLimitExceededError`"},"578":{"id":"/session/limits-37","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom-1","content":"`{ proceed: true, displace: null }`: allows the session without eviction (bypassing the limit)"},"579":{"id":"/session/limits-38","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom-1","content":"`{ proceed: true, displace: session }`: evicts that specific session and starts"},"580":{"id":"/session/limits-39","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#custom-1","content":"**Example:** An admin dashboard with max 3 per guild. On exceed, the custom handler replies with a queue\nstatus message and blocks the new session."},"581":{"id":"/session/limits-40","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#predicates","content":"When you need different limits for the same session type (e.g. premium vs free users), use predicates."},"582":{"id":"/session/limits-41","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#predicates","content":"If two or more policies for the same constructor match (or all lack a predicate), an `AmbiguousSessionLimitError` is thrown. Make sure predicates are mutually exclusive."},"583":{"id":"/session/limits-42","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#inheritance","content":"Limits are inherited through the prototype chain. When you start a child session, both the parent's and the child's policies are checked (AND semantics)."},"584":{"id":"/session/limits-43","page_id":"/session/limits","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/limits#multiple-rules","content":"A single policy can define multiple rules. All rules must pass for the session to start."},"585":{"id":"/session/middlewares","page_id":"/session/middlewares","type":"page","content":"Middlewares","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin","Other"],"tags":[],"url":"/session/middlewares"},"586":{"id":"/session/middlewares-0","page_id":"/session/middlewares","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/middlewares#usage","content":"Usage"},"587":{"id":"/session/middlewares-1","page_id":"/session/middlewares","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/middlewares#creation","content":"Creation"},"588":{"id":"/session/middlewares-2","page_id":"/session/middlewares","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/middlewares#registration","content":"Registration"},"589":{"id":"/session/middlewares-3","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares","content":"Middlewares are objects or callbacks that run before any session is executed. They can do some pre-processing logic and store it in the metadata, or even prevent the subscriber from being executed."},"590":{"id":"/session/middlewares-4","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares","content":"Specifically, sessions have two types of middlewares: one for starting sessions, and one for updating them."},"591":{"id":"/session/middlewares-5","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares","content":"For general information about middlewares, you must first read the general Middlewares guide."},"592":{"id":"/session/middlewares-6","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares#creation","content":"Either:"},"593":{"id":"/session/middlewares-7","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares#creation","content":"Create a class that extends `BaseSessionStartMiddleware` or `BaseSessionUpdateMiddleware` and implements the `check()` method."},"594":{"id":"/session/middlewares-8","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares#creation","content":"Create a function that returns a `MiddlewareResponse`."},"595":{"id":"/session/middlewares-9","page_id":"/session/middlewares","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/middlewares#registration","content":"Register it to the executor's `MiddlewareList`:"},"596":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","type":"page","content":"List Pagination Session","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin","Types"],"tags":[],"url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session"},"597":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-0","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#creation","content":"Creation"},"598":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-1","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#creation-1","content":"Creation"},"599":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-2","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#implementation","content":"Implementation"},"600":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-3","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#initialization","content":"Initialization"},"601":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-4","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#example","content":"Example"},"602":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-5","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">It's recommended to read the Pagination Session page first, all of its features apply to this.</Callout>"},"603":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-6","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","content":"A `ListPaginationSession` is a special type of pagination session made to paginate a list of items."},"604":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-7","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","content":"Initially, the item's values are received at the session's constructor. You can also include a refreshing system in the session to refresh the items with their newest state, if desired."},"605":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-8","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#creation-1","content":"Extend the `AbstractListPaginationSession` class:"},"606":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-9","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#creation-1","content":"The first type argument is the type of the items, and the second is the session's return type."},"607":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-10","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#creation-1","content":"In `updatePage()` you can now use `getCurrentPageItems()`, which is an utility method that calculates and returns the current page's items."},"608":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-11","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#implementation","content":"Implement it the same way you'd implement a `PaginationSession`."},"609":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-12","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#initialization","content":"Instantiate and start your session the same way as a regular one, but passing the list of items:"},"610":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-13","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#example","content":"This example will paginate a list of the currently cached guilds:"},"611":{"id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session-14","page_id":"/session/types/list-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/list-pagination-session#example","content":"You can then use it in your command or anywhere where you have an interaction:"},"612":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"page","content":"Pagination Session","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin","Types"],"tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session"},"613":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-0","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"Page switch"},"614":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-1","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session#creation","content":"Creation"},"615":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-2","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session#creation-1","content":"Creation"},"616":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-3","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session#implementation","content":"Implementation"},"617":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-4","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session#initialization","content":"Initialization"},"618":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-5","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"Pagination customId"},"619":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-6","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">It's recommended to read the Session page first, all of its features apply to this.</Callout>"},"620":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-7","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session","content":"A `PaginationSession` is a special type of session made to be paginated (have pages)."},"621":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-8","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session","content":"From a manager's perspective, a pagination session is just a regular session. The pagination logic happens inside the session\nitself."},"622":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-9","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"A page switch is triggered when the user sends an interaction to the pagination session, and a page can be extracted from it:"},"623":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-10","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"It attempts to extract a referred page, depending on the interaction type:Buttons: Extracts from the customId.Select Menu: Extracts from the customId. If no page is present there, and it's a `StringSelectMenu`, and only one value was selected, it extracts from the selected value.Modal: Extracts from the customId. If no page is present there, it iterates through the modal's components, searching for a component whose `customId` is the session's `customId`. If there is one, the page is extracted from said component's value."},"624":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-11","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"If there's no referred page, it behaves like a regular session, passing the interaction to the appropiate handler."},"625":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-12","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"If there's a referred page, it updates its `currentPage` and calls `#updatePage()`."},"626":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-13","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"You can override this behavior by overriding `extractPageFromInteraction()`, or the more concrete methods:"},"627":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-14","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"`extractPageFromButton()` for buttons"},"628":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-15","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"`extractPageFromSelectMenu()` for select menus"},"629":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-16","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#page-switch","content":"`extractPageFromModal()` for modals"},"630":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-17","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#creation-1","content":"Extend the `AbstractPaginationSession` class:"},"631":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-18","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#implementation","content":"Apart from the base `Session` implementation, also implement the `updatePage()` method:"},"632":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-19","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#implementation","content":"Similarly to `update()`, it must return whether the session's TTL should be renewed or not."},"633":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-20","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#initialization","content":"Instantiate and start your session the same way as a regular one:"},"634":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-21","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"The page to switch to is usually extracted from the customId. This means you'll need to change the way you build it in case you want to make a component that switches to a specific page."},"635":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-22","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"You can add more ways by overriding `extractPageFromButton()`."},"636":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-23","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"You can either:"},"637":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-24","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"Put the pagination custom id in the select menu itself, making it switch to that page regardless of selection."},"638":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-25","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"Put the pagination custom id in the select menu's options, making it switch to that page only when the option is selected.\nNote that you still need to put the session's custom id in the select menu itself."},"639":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-26","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"You can add more ways by overriding `extractPageFromSelectMenu()`."},"640":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-27","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"You can either:"},"641":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-28","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"Put the pagination custom id in the modal itself, making it switch to that page regardless of values."},"642":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-29","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"Put the session's custom id in the modal's components, making it switch to that component's value (if it's a number).\nNote that you still need to put the session's custom id in the modal."},"643":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-30","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">If the component's value is not a number, it will be handled as a regular update (`handleModal()`).</Callout>"},"644":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-31","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"The `AbstractPaginationSession` has a utility method for building an action row containing two buttons that switch to the previous and next page:"},"645":{"id":"/session/types/pagination-session-32","page_id":"/session/types/pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/pagination-session#pagination-customid","content":"This row uses emoji arrows to avoid issues with localized text."},"646":{"id":"/session/types/session","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"page","content":"Session","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin","Types"],"tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session"},"647":{"id":"/session/types/session-0","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#usage","content":"Usage"},"648":{"id":"/session/types/session-1","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#creation","content":"Creation"},"649":{"id":"/session/types/session-2","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#implementation","content":"Implementation"},"650":{"id":"/session/types/session-3","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#initialization","content":"Initialization"},"651":{"id":"/session/types/session-4","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#component-customids","content":"Component customIds"},"652":{"id":"/session/types/session-5","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#complex-data","content":"Complex data"},"653":{"id":"/session/types/session-6","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#session-lifecycle","content":"Session lifecycle"},"654":{"id":"/session/types/session-7","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#end-promise","content":"End promise"},"655":{"id":"/session/types/session-8","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#result","content":"Result"},"656":{"id":"/session/types/session-9","page_id":"/session/types/session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/session#metadata","content":"Metadata"},"657":{"id":"/session/types/session-10","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">It's recommended to read the Overview page first.</Callout>"},"658":{"id":"/session/types/session-11","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session","content":"A `Session` is the simplest, most generic object for the sessions API. It replies to interactions it receives and ends after a given TTL."},"659":{"id":"/session/types/session-12","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session","content":"Further session types are based on this one, and are specifically built for other common use cases."},"660":{"id":"/session/types/session-13","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#creation","content":"Extend the `AbstractSession` class:"},"661":{"id":"/session/types/session-14","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#creation","content":"There's an optional type argument which is the return type of your session, which will be explained later."},"662":{"id":"/session/types/session-15","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#implementation","content":"Implement the `onStart` and `onEnd` methods:"},"663":{"id":"/session/types/session-16","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#implementation","content":"Your `onStart` method should perform the initial reply, and `onEnd` any necessary cleanup logic."},"664":{"id":"/session/types/session-17","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#implementation","content":"If the `onStart` method errors, the session will not be registered and the `onEnd` method will not be called."},"665":{"id":"/session/types/session-18","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#implementation","content":"Optionally implement `handleButton`, `handleSelectMenu`, and `handleModal` methods to listen to interactions:"},"666":{"id":"/session/types/session-19","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#initialization","content":"Somewhere in your code where you want to start a session, create an id for it, instantiate and start the session:"},"667":{"id":"/session/types/session-20","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#initialization","content":"In production your ID should be randomly generated using something like nanoid, and it should be short enough to not collide with extra customId data."},"668":{"id":"/session/types/session-21","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#initialization","content":"You can use nanoid's collission calculator to find out how short your ID needs to be.\nConsider a collision only happens if two **currently active** sessions have the same ID."},"669":{"id":"/session/types/session-22","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#component-customids","content":"Given sessions aren't limited to a single `Message`, and the framework needs to know to which session a given component belongs to, you'll need to go through the `buildCustomId` method in order to get your customIds.\nThis will append the necessary information to the customId to allow the framework to know how to route the interaction."},"670":{"id":"/session/types/session-23","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#component-customids","content":"You can also append extra data to it by passing it to the method, and it will be saved in the `TypedFields.CustomIdExtra` field."},"671":{"id":"/session/types/session-24","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#complex-data","content":"If you need to store a complex object as extra data you can consider using the `@sapphire/string-store` package, which is what\nthe framework and plugin already uses for serialization to short strings:"},"672":{"id":"/session/types/session-25","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#complex-data","content":"Check their documentation for more information and examples."},"673":{"id":"/session/types/session-26","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#session-lifecycle","content":"After it's started, a session will have a given TTL before ending. The default is 3 minutes, and it can be overriden per session (in milliseconds):"},"674":{"id":"/session/types/session-27","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#session-lifecycle","content":"When the session receives an interaction, it can decide whether or not to renew its TTL by returning `true` on the appropiate handler (or `false` to not renew it):"},"675":{"id":"/session/types/session-28","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#session-lifecycle","content":"This is useful to \"filter out\" interactions that you don't want to renew the TTL of, like from other users or with invalid input."},"676":{"id":"/session/types/session-29","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#end-promise","content":"Sessions are asynchronous by nature, and you may want to wait for a session to finish before continuing. The `getEndPromise()` method returns a promise that resolves when the session ends, either by timeout or manual end."},"677":{"id":"/session/types/session-30","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#end-promise","content":"This promise resolves to an  object containing the session's final state and result:"},"678":{"id":"/session/types/session-31","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#end-promise","content":"This is particularly useful when you want to perform additional actions after a session completes, such as logging, notifications, or cleanup operations."},"679":{"id":"/session/types/session-32","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#result","content":"Sessions can specify a `result` that will be passed to awaiters of the session's promise, and the session end event:"},"680":{"id":"/session/types/session-33","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#result","content":"The default value of the `result` is `null`, which is what consumers will receive if you don't set it."},"681":{"id":"/session/types/session-34","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#result","content":"The `onEnd()` method will be called **before** the framework gets the result from the session, so you can use it to make some final changes to it,\nbefore it's communicated to the consumer."},"682":{"id":"/session/types/session-35","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#result","content":"Then you can await the session's promise to get the result:"},"683":{"id":"/session/types/session-36","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#result","content":"A useful use case is to make sessions where a user is \"building\" something, and you want to get the final result the user inputted."},"684":{"id":"/session/types/session-37","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#metadata","content":"When extending with plugins, you may want to specify extra data for them to read. You can do so with the `Metadata` object, saved on the session."},"685":{"id":"/session/types/session-38","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#metadata","content":"While sessions internally save a `Metadata`, the return type of `#getMeta()` is a `ReadonlyMetadata`,\nmeaning that external objects can read the object, but not modify it."},"686":{"id":"/session/types/session-39","page_id":"/session/types/session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/session#metadata","content":"For a more type-safe approach, you can use `TypedFields`. Check the Metadata page for more information."},"687":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"page","content":"Stage Pagination Session","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Session Plugin","Types"],"tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session"},"688":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-0","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"Stages"},"689":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-1","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#pagination","content":"Pagination"},"690":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-2","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#creation","content":"Creation"},"691":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-3","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#start-stage-creation","content":"Start stage creation"},"692":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-4","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#class-creation","content":"Class creation"},"693":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-5","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"Implementation"},"694":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-6","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages-creation","content":"Stages creation"},"695":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-7","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#class-creation-1","content":"Class creation"},"696":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-8","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-1","content":"Implementation"},"697":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-9","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#session-creation","content":"Session creation"},"698":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-10","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#class-creation-2","content":"Class creation"},"699":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-11","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-2","content":"Implementation"},"700":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-12","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#initialization","content":"Initialization"},"701":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-13","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">It's recommended to read the Pagination Session page first, all of its features apply to this.</Callout>"},"702":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-14","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","content":"A `StagePaginationSession` is a special type of pagination session made to paginate a list of stages."},"703":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-15","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"A stage is an object inside a `StagePaginationSession` that represents a single page in the pagination. You can view them as a \"nested\" session."},"704":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-16","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"Switching from one stage to another is the equivalent of switching pages on a pagination component."},"705":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-17","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"A stage can:"},"706":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-18","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"Be updated, similar to a `Session` update."},"707":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-19","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"Be switched to and reply to the interaction switching to it."},"708":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-20","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"Be left and perform some cleanup logic."},"709":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-21","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"Return a result, similar to a `Session` result."},"710":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-22","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages","content":"The first stage is a `SessionStartStage`. It behaves exactly the same as any other, except it also has a `SessionStartStage#onStart()` method."},"711":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-23","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#pagination","content":"The pagination works in a similar way as in the `PaginationSession`. In essence:"},"712":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-24","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#pagination","content":"A customId not referring to a page is handled by `#update()` of the current stage."},"713":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-25","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#pagination","content":"A customId referring to a page makes the session switch to that stage, calling `SessionStage#onSwitch()` on the new one and `SessionStage#onLeave()` on the old one."},"714":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-26","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#creation","content":"There are three things you need to build to create a full `StagePaginationSession`:"},"715":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-27","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#creation","content":"The start stage"},"716":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-28","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#creation","content":"The stages (at least one)"},"717":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-29","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#creation","content":"The session"},"718":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-30","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#start-stage-creation","content":"You'll first need to build the first stage of the session, a `SessionStartStage`."},"719":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-31","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#class-creation","content":"Extend the `AbstractSessionStartStage` class:"},"720":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-32","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"Implement:"},"721":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-33","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"`onStart()`: Replies to the start interaction."},"722":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-34","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"`onSwitch()`: Replies to the interaction when the user switches to this stage."},"723":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-35","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"`onLeave()`: Performs some cleanup logic when the user leaves the stage."},"724":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-36","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">You should not reply to the `onLeave()` interaction, as this will be done by the next stage.</Callout>"},"725":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-37","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation","content":"The type argument is the return type of your stage, which will be explained later."},"726":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-38","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#stages-creation","content":"After the first stage, you can create as many stages as you want."},"727":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-39","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#class-creation-1","content":"Extend the `AbstractSessionStage` class:"},"728":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-40","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-1","content":"Implement:"},"729":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-41","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-1","content":"`onSwitch()`: Replies to the interaction when the user switches to this stage."},"730":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-42","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-1","content":"`onLeave()`: Performs some cleanup logic when the user leaves the stage."},"731":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-43","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-1","content":"<Callout type=\"warn\">You should not reply to the `onLeave()` interaction, as this will be done by the next stage.</Callout>"},"732":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-44","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#session-creation","content":"After all stages are created, you can create the session."},"733":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-45","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#class-creation-2","content":"Extend the `AbstractStagePaginationSession` class:"},"734":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-46","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#implementation-2","content":"Implement `onEnd()` and `stages`:"},"735":{"id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session-47","page_id":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/session/types/stage-pagination-session#initialization","content":"Instantiate and start your session the same way as a regular one:"},"736":{"id":"/typed-options","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Typed Options"],"tags":[],"url":"/typed-options"},"737":{"id":"/typed-options-0","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options#installation","content":"Installation"},"738":{"id":"/typed-options-1","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options#installing","content":"Installing"},"739":{"id":"/typed-options-2","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options#defining-the-command","content":"Defining the command"},"740":{"id":"/typed-options-3","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options#reading-the-options","content":"Reading the options"},"741":{"id":"/typed-options-4","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options#entry-points","content":"Entry points"},"742":{"id":"/typed-options-5","page_id":"/typed-options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options#using-it-in-a-nyx-command","content":"Using it in a nyx command"},"743":{"id":"/typed-options-6","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options","content":"The `@nyx-discord/typed-options` package types\nthe options of your slash commands from the command data itself, so a misspelled name, a wrong option kind or\na missing `null` check becomes a compile error."},"744":{"id":"/typed-options-7","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options","content":"Without it, `interaction.options.getString('reason')` accepts any name, ignores `required` and `choices`, and returns\n`string | null` even for options Discord always sends. With it, the getters are checked against the data you already write."},"745":{"id":"/typed-options-8","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options","content":"It doesn't depend on the rest of nyx: it only needs `discord-api-types`. You can use it in any bot that uses discord.js, `@discordjs/core` or raw API payloads, with or without nyx."},"746":{"id":"/typed-options-9","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#installing","content":"It has `discord-api-types` as a peer dependency, and `discord.js` as an optional one for the `/djs` entry point."},"747":{"id":"/typed-options-10","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#defining-the-command","content":"Create the command data with `chatInput()` and one helper per option kind. The result is plain API JSON, so you register it with any library, or use it as the `data` of a nyx command:"},"748":{"id":"/typed-options-11","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#reading-the-options","content":"Pass the data and the interaction to `typedOptions()`. The entry point you import it from depends on your library:"},"749":{"id":"/typed-options-12","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#reading-the-options","content":"A mistake in the name, or in the kind of option, doesn't compile:"},"750":{"id":"/typed-options-13","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#entry-points","content":"| Entry point                  | Purpose                                                                                                                            |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@nyx-discord/typed-options` | `chatInput()`, `subcommand()`, `group()`, the option helpers, and the types of the getters. Doesn't depend on any Discord library. |","table":"table-0"},"751":{"id":"/typed-options-14","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#entry-points","content":"| Entry point                      | Purpose                                                                                                                |\n| -------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@nyx-discord/typed-options/djs` | `typedOptions()` for discord.js. It returns `interaction.options` with narrower types, so it costs nothing at runtime. |","table":"table-0"},"752":{"id":"/typed-options-15","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#entry-points","content":"| Entry point                           | Purpose                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@nyx-discord/typed-options/djs-core` | `typedOptions()` for raw API payloads. It takes the `@discordjs/core` event props or a bare interaction payload, so it also covers the HTTP transport and other libraries. |","table":"table-0"},"753":{"id":"/typed-options-16","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#using-it-in-a-nyx-command","content":"Read the options from the command's own data:"},"754":{"id":"/typed-options-17","page_id":"/typed-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options#using-it-in-a-nyx-command","content":"Builders like `SlashCommandBuilder` can't carry literal types, so they keep working but aren't typed. Use `chatInput()` for the commands whose options you want checked."},"755":{"id":"/typed-options/options","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"page","content":"Options","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Typed Options","Options"],"tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options"},"756":{"id":"/typed-options/options-0","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options#required-options","content":"Required options"},"757":{"id":"/typed-options/options-1","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options#choices","content":"Choices"},"758":{"id":"/typed-options/options-2","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options#users-and-members","content":"Users and members"},"759":{"id":"/typed-options/options-3","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options#channels","content":"Channels"},"760":{"id":"/typed-options/options-4","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options#mentionables","content":"Mentionables"},"761":{"id":"/typed-options/options-5","page_id":"/typed-options/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/options#raw-payloads","content":"Raw payloads"},"762":{"id":"/typed-options/options-6","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"Each option is defined with a helper, under the name it will have in Discord. The helpers take the same fields as the API (`description`, `required`, `choices`, `min_value`...), and `typedOptions()` gives you one getter per option kind."},"763":{"id":"/typed-options/options-7","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper     | Getter        | Returns  |\n| ---------- | ------------- | -------- |\n| `string()` | `getString()` | `string` |","table":"table-0"},"764":{"id":"/typed-options/options-8","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper      | Getter         | Returns  |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------- |\n| `integer()` | `getInteger()` | `number` |","table":"table-0"},"765":{"id":"/typed-options/options-9","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper     | Getter        | Returns  |\n| ---------- | ------------- | -------- |\n| `number()` | `getNumber()` | `number` |","table":"table-0"},"766":{"id":"/typed-options/options-10","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper      | Getter         | Returns   |\n| ----------- | -------------- | --------- |\n| `boolean()` | `getBoolean()` | `boolean` |","table":"table-0"},"767":{"id":"/typed-options/options-11","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper   | Getter                     | Returns                  |\n| -------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `user()` | `getUser()`, `getMember()` | The user, and the member |","table":"table-0"},"768":{"id":"/typed-options/options-12","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper      | Getter         | Returns     |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ----------- |\n| `channel()` | `getChannel()` | The channel |","table":"table-0"},"769":{"id":"/typed-options/options-13","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper   | Getter      | Returns  |\n| -------- | ----------- | -------- |\n| `role()` | `getRole()` | The role |","table":"table-0"},"770":{"id":"/typed-options/options-14","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper          | Getter             | Returns                |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------- |\n| `mentionable()` | `getMentionable()` | A user, member or role |","table":"table-0"},"771":{"id":"/typed-options/options-15","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"| Helper         | Getter            | Returns        |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | -------------- |\n| `attachment()` | `getAttachment()` | The attachment |","table":"table-0"},"772":{"id":"/typed-options/options-16","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options","content":"Every getter only accepts the names of options of its own kind. What it returns is the same as in your library, so `getUser()` returns a `User` on discord.js and an `APIUser` with raw payloads."},"773":{"id":"/typed-options/options-17","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#required-options","content":"A getter returns `null` unless the option is `required: true`, in which case Discord always sends it and the type is not nullable:"},"774":{"id":"/typed-options/options-18","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#choices","content":"When an option has `choices`, the getter returns the union of their values:"},"775":{"id":"/typed-options/options-19","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#users-and-members","content":"A `user()` option resolves to a user, but the user might not be in the guild (or the command might run in a DM), so `getMember()` is **always** nullable, even for required options:"},"776":{"id":"/typed-options/options-20","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#channels","content":"`channel_types` narrows the channel the getter returns:"},"777":{"id":"/typed-options/options-21","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#mentionables","content":"`getMentionable()` returns the union of what a mentionable can be: a user, a member or a role. Use `getMember()` and `getRole()` for the other kinds' own options."},"778":{"id":"/typed-options/options-22","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#raw-payloads","content":"With `@nyx-discord/typed-options/djs-core` there is no library to resolve the options for you, so `typedOptions()` reads them from the payload and looks up the users, members, channels, roles and attachments in `resolved` by their ID. Options missing from the payload are `null`:"},"779":{"id":"/typed-options/options-23","page_id":"/typed-options/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/options#raw-payloads","content":"It takes the interaction payload itself, or the `@discordjs/core` event props that wrap it as `data`, so it works the same for the gateway, for HTTP bots and for any other library."},"780":{"id":"/typed-options/subcommands","page_id":"/typed-options/subcommands","type":"page","content":"Subcommands","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Typed Options","Options"],"tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/subcommands"},"781":{"id":"/typed-options/subcommands-0","page_id":"/typed-options/subcommands","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/typed-options/subcommands#reading-a-subcommands-options","content":"Reading a subcommand's options"},"782":{"id":"/typed-options/subcommands-1","page_id":"/typed-options/subcommands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/subcommands","content":"A command with subcommands has no options of its own, so `chatInput()` takes a list of `subcommands` instead. Create each one with `subcommand()`, and group them with `group()`:"},"783":{"id":"/typed-options/subcommands-2","page_id":"/typed-options/subcommands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/subcommands#reading-a-subcommands-options","content":"Subcommand and group names are typed as `string`, so which subcommand ran is not inferred from the interaction. Instead, pass **the subcommand's own data** to `typedOptions()` to type its options:"},"784":{"id":"/typed-options/subcommands-3","page_id":"/typed-options/subcommands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/subcommands#reading-a-subcommands-options","content":"This fits nyx's subcommands, which already live in their own class: define the subcommand's data there and read the options from it."},"785":{"id":"/typed-options/subcommands-4","page_id":"/typed-options/subcommands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/typed-options/subcommands#reading-a-subcommands-options","content":"With raw payloads, `typedOptions()` finds the options inside the subcommand (and its group) for you."},"786":{"id":"/use/commands/components","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"page","content":"Components","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Use","Commands"],"tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components"},"787":{"id":"/use/commands/components-0","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#usage","content":"Usage"},"788":{"id":"/use/commands/components-1","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#bot-extraction","content":"Bot extraction"},"789":{"id":"/use/commands/components-2","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#component-creation","content":"Component creation"},"790":{"id":"/use/commands/components-3","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#interaction-handling","content":"Interaction handling"},"791":{"id":"/use/commands/components-4","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#attaching-extra-data","content":"Attaching extra data"},"792":{"id":"/use/commands/components-5","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#complex-data","content":"Complex data"},"793":{"id":"/use/commands/components-6","page_id":"/use/commands/components","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/commands/components#referring-to-other-commands","content":"Referring to other commands"},"794":{"id":"/use/commands/components-7","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components","content":"You can make your components sent by your commands trigger a callback in the command itself, instead of having to listen to `interactionCreate` separately."},"795":{"id":"/use/commands/components-8","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components","content":"This is only recommended for simple non complex components that originate directly from a command.\nFor other cases, create an `interactionCreate` subscriber."},"796":{"id":"/use/commands/components-9","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components","content":"Given only these are executable, you can only use this in Standalone Commands, SubCommands and Context Menu Commands."},"797":{"id":"/use/commands/components-10","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components#usage","content":"In this example we'll use a standalone command, but the same applies to the rest."},"798":{"id":"/use/commands/components-11","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components#bot-extraction","content":"You'll first need your bot instance, since it contains the codec used to de/serialize the customIds."},"799":{"id":"/use/commands/components-12","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components#bot-extraction","content":"You can either instantiate your command with it, or get it from the execution metadata:"},"800":{"id":"/use/commands/components-13","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/commands/components#bot-extraction","content":"To learn more about TypedFields, check the Metadata page."},"801":{"id":"/use/commands/components-14","page_id":"/use/commands/components","tags":[