uses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#subscriber-concurrency","content":"Subscriber concurrency"},"1030":{"id":"/use/events/buses-2","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#async-buses","content":"Async buses"},"1031":{"id":"/use/events/buses-3","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#concurrency-limit","content":"Concurrency Limit"},"1032":{"id":"/use/events/buses-4","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#sync-buses","content":"Sync buses"},"1033":{"id":"/use/events/buses-5","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#sync-timeout","content":"Sync Timeout"},"1034":{"id":"/use/events/buses-6","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#known-buses","content":"Known buses"},"1035":{"id":"/use/events/buses-7","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#client-bus","content":"Client bus"},"1036":{"id":"/use/events/buses-8","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#manager-buses","content":"Manager buses"},"1037":{"id":"/use/events/buses-9","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#custom-buses","content":"Custom buses"},"1038":{"id":"/use/events/buses-10","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#arguments-type","content":"Arguments type"},"1039":{"id":"/use/events/buses-11","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#creation","content":"Creation"},"1040":{"id":"/use/events/buses-12","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#manual-emits","content":"Manual emits"},"1041":{"id":"/use/events/buses-13","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#from-an-eventemitter","content":"From an EventEmitter"},"1042":{"id":"/use/events/buses-14","page_id":"/use/events/buses","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/use/events/buses#bus-events","content":"Bus events"},"1043":{"id":"/use/events/buses-15","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses","content":"Event buses are objects that store and notify their `EventSubscribers` when an event is called either internally, typically via an EventEmitter, or externally, via `EventBus#emit()`."},"1044":{"id":"/use/events/buses-16","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#main-features","content":"An event bus can be un/subscribed to:"},"1045":{"id":"/use/events/buses-17","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#main-features","content":"Can be used to emit an event type-safely:"},"1046":{"id":"/use/events/buses-18","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#main-features","content":"It can be iterated and its subscribers can be obtained:"},"1047":{"id":"/use/events/buses-19","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#main-features","content":"And other features you might find useful. Check the  for more details."},"1048":{"id":"/use/events/buses-20","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#subscriber-concurrency","content":"An event bus has complete freedom over how to execute its subscribers, however the framework has normalized two patterns for ease of use (though it's not hardcoded):"},"1049":{"id":"/use/events/buses-21","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#async-buses","content":"It calls its subscribers asynchronously, meaning that it doesn't wait for the current subscriber to finish before executing the next."},"1050":{"id":"/use/events/buses-22","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#async-buses","content":"| Advantages                                                                                  | Disadvantages                                                                 |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Can be faster, especially for events with many subscribers, since it executes them in bulk. | Multiple subscribers running may hog the event loop and decrease performance. |","table":"table-0"},"1051":{"id":"/use/events/buses-23","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#async-buses","content":"| Advantages                                                                                                                            | Disadvantages                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Less prone to blocking or delaying the system, since it can move on to the next subscriber while the previous one is still executing. | May lead to calling subscribers in an order different than their priority. For example, subscribers with `PriorityEnum.Normal` may execute before subscribers with `PriorityEnum.High` have finished. |","table":"table-0"},"1052":{"id":"/use/events/buses-24","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#async-buses","content":"| Advantages | Disadvantages                                                                           |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|            | Since subscribers are executed in bulk, it can be harder to trace when an error occurs. |","table":"table-0"},"1053":{"id":"/use/events/buses-25","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#concurrency-limit","content":"To tackle the mentioned disadvantages, it has a concurrency limit functionality. This allows you to set how many subscribers are being checked or executed at the same time."},"1054":{"id":"/use/events/buses-26","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#concurrency-limit","content":"Setting this limit to `1` effectively turns the dispatcher into a sync one."},"1055":{"id":"/use/events/buses-27","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#concurrency-limit","content":"The default concurrency limit is `3`."},"1056":{"id":"/use/events/buses-28","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#sync-buses","content":"It calls its subscribers synchronously, meaning that it waits for the current subscriber to finish before executing the next."},"1057":{"id":"/use/events/buses-29","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#sync-buses","content":"| Advantages                                                                   | Disadvantages                                                                                                                                          |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Ensures that subscribers are only executed in the order of their `Priority`. | May be slower for events with many subscribers, as it has to wait for each subscriber (and its middleware) to finish before moving on to the next one. |","table":"table-1"},"1058":{"id":"/use/events/buses-30","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#sync-buses","content":"| Advantages                                                            | Disadvantages                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Easier to debug and to trace when and on which state an error occurs. | If one subscriber takes a long time to execute, it can cause a delay for others. |","table":"table-1"},"1059":{"id":"/use/events/buses-31","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#sync-timeout","content":"To tackle the mentioned disadvantages, it has a sync timeout functionality. This allows you to set \"timeframe\" for any subscriber to finish, before the dispatcher stops waiting and calls the next subscriber."},"1060":{"id":"/use/events/buses-32","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#sync-timeout","content":"<Callout>The default is of 10000 ms (10 seconds).</Callout>"},"1061":{"id":"/use/events/buses-33","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#client-bus","content":"The `Client` event bus is a built-in bus that wraps its events:"},"1062":{"id":"/use/events/buses-34","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#client-bus","content":"The bot also has a utility method to directly subscribe to it:"},"1063":{"id":"/use/events/buses-35","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#manager-buses","content":"Each manager holds a bus that wraps events related to the feature they manage:"},"1064":{"id":"/use/events/buses-36","page_id":"/use/events/buses","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/use/events/buses#manager-buses","con