er`: Resolves the command that a given command interaction refers to."],[147,"`CommandSubscriptionsContainer`: Stores the subscribers that are subscribed to the client's `EventBus` to listen for command interactions."],[230,"`EventBus`: Stores subscribers and emits events."],[229,"`EventDispatcher`: Coordinates middleware checks and subscriber execution for each dispatch."],[231,"`EventSubscriber`: Receives events and executes logic."],[909,"`executeMessage()` for message context menus."],[910,"`executeUser()` for user context menus."],[627,"`extractPageFromButton()` for buttons"],[629,"`extractPageFromModal()` for modals"],[628,"`extractPageFromSelectMenu()` for select menus"],[1480,"`false()` - The middleware fails, and the execution will stop."],[457,"`filter`"],[1481,"`forceTrue()` - The middleware forces to pass, even if other later middlewares would fail."],[777,"`getMentionable()` returns the union of what a mentionable can be: a user, a member or a role. Use `getMember()` and `getRole()` for the other kinds' own options."],[803,"`handleButton` for buttons"],[805,"`handleModal` for modals"],[804,"`handleSelectMenu` for select menus"],[1145,"`HighMonitor` is the first priority to be executed."],[1474,"`HighMonitor` is the first priority to be executed."],[1223,"`HttpBot.create()` works like `@nyx-discord/djs-core`'s `Bot.create()`, but takes your application's ID and public key (both on the Developer Portal) instead of a client, and creates the client for you. `Bot` from `@nyx-discord/http` is `HttpBot`, so examples using `Bot.create()` or the `Bot` type work as-is:"],[1277,"`HttpBot` sets this up for you. If you create the `HttpNyxClient` yourself, add the field to the client event bus once the bot is created:"],[1146,"`LowMonitor` is the last priority to be executed."],[1475,"`LowMonitor` is the last priority to be executed."],[1164,"`On` to \"permanently\" subscribe to the bus until manually unsubscribed (default)."],[1165,"`Once` to subscribe for a single 