ant to...                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Use a different timing/job backend (not `croner`) through a custom `ScheduleExecutionScheduler`. | Change only schedule storage or execution behavior. Those are responsibilities of `ScheduleRepository` and `ScheduleExecutor`. |"],[375,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                                | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Enforce custom consistency/uniqueness rules at storage level (e.g., dedup by business key). | Change middleware flow or pre-execution checks. That belongs to `ScheduleMiddlewareList`. |"],[71,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                            | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                           |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Customize how commands are located from the repository when an interaction is received. | Introduce other localization methods. It's easier to make your own method that uses the `CommandRepository`. |"],[281,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                            | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                           |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Support a different interval format or next-run strategy (e.g., RRULE-like scheduling). | Change schedule execution logic (try/catch, retry, middleware behavior). That belongs to `ScheduleExecutor`. |"],[347,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                          | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Adapt a third-party scheduler/queue API to Nyx's `pause`/`resume`/`destroy` contract. | Only change interval parsing or next-run calculation. That belongs to `ScheduleExecutionScheduler`. |"],[376,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                      | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                     |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Support multi-tenant partitioning or custom query/filter capabilities in storage. | Change manager event orchestration. That belongs to `ScheduleManager`. |"],[297,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                    | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Customize execution behavior, including middleware injection or error handling. | Only change the middleware chain. Use `ScheduleMiddlewareList` for that. |"],[166,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                 | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                    |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change fallback behavior for uncaught errors (logging, telemetry, alerting). | Change middleware order. Use the dispatcher middleware list for that. |"],[316,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                                | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                 |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change fallback behavior for uncaught errors, such as logging or telemetry. | Change when schedules run. That's done with `ScheduleExecutionScheduler` and `ScheduleJobAdapter`. |"],[299,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                               | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Implement custom retry/backoff or exception mapping for failed executions. | Change when schedules run. That belongs to `ScheduleExecutionScheduler` and `ScheduleJobAdapter`. |"],[197,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                            | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Add custom logic that modify execution (instrumentation, retries, etc). | Add/change error consumers only. You can do that from the dispatcher's error handler. |"],[282,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                           | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                 |\n| ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Implement custom misfire/catch-up behavior for delayed or missed runs. | Change schedule persistence. That belongs to `ScheduleRepository`. |"],[334,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                          | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                 |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Enforce middleware deduplication or identity-based replacement rules. | Change when schedules are triggered. That belongs to `ScheduleExecutionScheduler`. |"],[333,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                         | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                       |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Add priority/group ordering semantics beyond simple insertion order. | Change error handling around `tick()` execution. That belongs to `ScheduleErrorHandler`. |"],[298,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                         | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                        |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Instrument executor-owned branches such as success/failure handling. | Only change how errors are consumed. Use `ScheduleErrorHandler` for that. |"],[280,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                        | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Use a different timing library or job backend (e.g., not `croner`). | Just adjust the job adapter itself. Create a custom `ScheduleJobAdapter` instead. |"],[120,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                       | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Add advanced logic while executing a command, like delaying calls. | Add new middlewares or error consumers. You can interact with the `MiddlewareList` and `ErrorHandler` objects directly, using the getter on the executor. |"],[374,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                       | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change schedule persistence (e.g., database instead of in-memory). | Adjust schedule execution or job lifecycle. Use `ScheduleExecutor` or `ScheduleJobAdapter` instead. |"],[196,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                       | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change how subscribers are dispatched (batching, throttling, etc). | Add/remove event middlewares only. You can do that from the dispatcher's middleware list. |"],[182,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                                    | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Replace the default middleware chain globally for a dispatcher. | Override all dispatcher logic. If only middleware behavior changes, replacing the list is enough. |"],[72,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                              | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                         |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| You need to perform extra logic while locating a command. | Deserialize `customIds` in different ways. That would be the `CommandCustomIdCodec`'s job. |"],[105,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                              | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                        |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Do something before, while or after checking middlewares. | Add new middlewares. The list already supports add and remove operations. |"],[317,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                           | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                               |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Route specific error classes to specialized consumers. | Replace the dispatch flow entirely. If you only want custom error handling, replacing this dependency is enough. |"],[167,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                           | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Route specific error classes to specialized consumers. | Replace dispatch flow entirely. If you only want custom error handling, replacing this dependency is enough. |"],[181,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                          | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                      |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change how middleware errors are wrapped or reported. | Handle subscriber errors. Use the dispatcher's `ErrorHandler` for that. |"],[180,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                        | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                              |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Add custom behavior before/after middleware checks. | Change subscriber execution order. That's controlled by the bus and its sorter. |"],[332,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                      | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Customize how middlewares are stored or iterated. | Add middlewares to the existing list. Use a custom `ScheduleExecutor` if you only need different injections. |"],[213,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                      | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                   |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Wrap a new event source (e.g. Redis, WebSockets). | Change how subscribers are called (use a custom Dispatcher instead). |"],[214,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                    | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                 |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change how subscribers are stored or retrieved. | Filter events globally (use a Middleware instead). |"],[106,"| ✅ Override if you want to...                   | ❌ Don't override if you want to... |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| Check middlewares in a different way or order. |                                    |"],[165,"| ✅ Override if you want to...               | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Resolve error consumers with custom logic. | Add/remove subscribers from buses. That's done with `EventBus#subscribe()` and `EventBus#unsubscribe()`. |"],[315,"| ✅ Override if you want to...               | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Resolve error consumers with custom logic. | Add or remove middlewares. That's done with the executor's middleware list. |"],[91,"| ✅ Override if you want to...              | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                 |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Resolve consumers with a different logic. | Add new consumers or a fallback one. The object already supports these operations. |"],[14,"| ✅ Override if you want to...         | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Use a custom de/serialization logic. | De/serialize your extra data. You should do that on sending/receiving instead, as it'll be easier to maintain. |"],[119,"| ✅ Override if you want to...         | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                           |\n| ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Customize how commands are executed. | Listen for command runs. Use the `EventBus` in the `CommandManager` instead. |"],[27,"| ✅ Override if you want to...        | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                                                                     |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Deploy commands in a different way. | Change command serialization. That is done in the command itself, you can override your `data` property or `getData()` method instead. |"],[58,"| ✅ Override if you want to...    | ❌ Don't override if you want to...                                                           |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Change how commands are stored. | Do something when commands are added, including decorating them. Use Command Events instead. |"],[121,"| ✅ Override if you want to... | ❌ Don't override if you want to...       